title: Syndrome of Inappropriate Secretion of ADH
---

# Syndrome of Inappropriate Secretion of ADH

- **Definition** - inappropriate secretion of ADH (either cerebral or tumour-derived) despite normovolaemia, normo- or hypo- osmoality, resulting in inappropriate free water retention
- **Etiology of SIADH:**
  - <u>Tumours</u> - particularly carcinomas (bronchogenic, duodenal, pancreas, bladder, prostate), haematological malignancies, thymoma, mesothelioma
  - <u>Pulmonary disorders</u> - pneumonia, tuberculosis, obstructive lung disease
  - <u>CNS disorders</u> - stroke, TBI, infection, psychosis, porphyria
  - <u>Drugs</u> - anticonvulsants, psychotropics, antidepressants, cytotoxics, oral hypoglycaemic agents, opiates
  - <u>Idiopathic</u>
- **Dx of SIADH** - demonstration of inappropriate diuresis and exclusion of other causes:
  - **Hypotonic hyponatraemia** - Na \< 130 mmol/L, serum osmolality \< 270 mOsm
  - **Inappropriate antidiuresis** - urine Osm \> 150, urine Na \> 30
  - **Exclusion of other causes** - e.g. TFT, early morning cortisol

  
  ![](../img/causes_and_dx_of_siadh.png)
- **Mx:**
  - Fluid restriction - 600-1000 ml/d
  - Tx of underlying cause if possible - e.g. withdrawal of precipitating drug
  - V2 antagonist - demeclocycline (600-900 mg/d)
